        { id: "s16", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s17", label: "Related Topics" },
        { id: "s18", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">

<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">The first dedicated US GAAP model for environmental credit markets</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">ASC 818 ESTABLISHES a DEDICATED accounting MODEL for RECOGNIZING, measuring, PRESENTING, and DISCLOSING environmental CREDITS and environmental CREDIT obligations (ECOs). AS more companies BECOME subject to REGULATORY compliance PROGRAMS, enter EMISSIONS reduction COMMITMENTS, and INVEST in renewable ENERGY, accounting for CARBON offsets, ALLOWANCES, and CREDITS had grown INCREASINGLY complex – WITHOUT any DEDICATED US GAAP guidance, COMPANIES had developed DIVERSE, inconsistent PRACTICES (analogizing to INVENTORY, intangible ASSETS, or CONTINGENCIES models). ASC 818 RESOLVES this by establishing ONE authoritative FRAMEWORK.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope – Defining Environmental Credits and ECOs</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Enforceable rights arising in a variety of forms</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">ENVIRONMENTAL credits are DEFINED as ENFORCEABLE rights that are ACQUIRED, internally GENERATED, granted BY a regulatory AGENCY, or RECEIVED in a NONRECIPROCAL transfer – EXISTING in a VARIETY of forms (CREDITS, certificates, ALLOWANCES, offsets), OFTEN used to SATISFY regulatory COMPLIANCE requirements. ASC 818 applies ONLY to environmental CREDITS and ECOs MEETING these SPECIFIC definitions.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>What Falls Outside the Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Income tax credits are explicitly excluded</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small);color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">ANY income TAX credits that MAY be used to SETTLE an ENTITY'S income TAX liability, REGARDLESS of WHETHER the entity HAS a tax LIABILITY or INTENDS to use the CREDIT for that PURPOSE, are SCOPED OUT of ASC 818 entirely – SUCH credits REMAIN governed by EXISTING income tax ACCOUNTING guidance, RATHER than this NEW environmental-credit-SPECIFIC model.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Recognition of Environmental Credits – Driven by Intended Use</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Recognition depends on what the entity plans to do with the credit</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small);color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">ENVIRONMENTAL credits PROBABLE of BEING used to SETTLE an ECO, or TRANSFERRED in an EXCHANGE transaction (e.g. a SALE or TRADE), are RECOGNIZED as an ASSET. THE cost of ALL other environmental CREDITS (e.g. VOLUNTARY credits held WITHOUT a probable SETTLEMENT or EXCHANGE intention) is EXPENSED as INCURRED – a GENUINELY significant recognition GATE, driven by MANAGEMENT'S intent RATHER than purely the CREDIT'S legal or CONTRACTUAL characteristics.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Measurement of Environmental Credits</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Measurement basis depends on how the credit was obtained</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.8fr;"><span>Method of obtaining</span><span>Measurement basis</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.8fr;"><span>Internally generated</span><span>TRANSACTION costs INCURRED to OBTAIN them</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.8fr;"><span>Received via nonreciprocal transfer (a grant)</span><span>TRANSACTION costs INCURRED to OBTAIN them</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.8fr;"><span>Received via reciprocal transfer (purchased)</span><span>COST</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Compliance Credits – Cost, With No Subsequent Remeasurement</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A stable, cost-based carrying value once recognized</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small);color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">ENVIRONMENTAL credits PROBABLE of BEING used to SETTLE an ECO (i.e. "COMPLIANCE" environmental CREDITS) are RECOGNIZED at COST, WITH NO subsequent REMEASUREMENT – the CARRYING amount REMAINS fixed at ITS initial cost BASIS going FORWARD, UNLIKE fair-VALUE-driven asset CATEGORIES elsewhere in US GAAP.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Non-Compliance Credits Recognized as Assets – Impairment Testing</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A cost-with-impairment model for exchange-intended credits</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small);color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">CREDITS recognized as ASSETS because they are PROBABLE of BEING transferred in an EXCHANGE transaction (RATHER than used for COMPLIANCE) are ALSO recognized at COST, but ARE tested for IMPAIRMENT at EACH reporting DATE – a MEANINGFUL distinction from the COMPLIANCE credit TREATMENT (Section 6), WHICH is NEVER remeasured at ALL.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Recognition and Measurement of Environmental Credit Obligations (ECOs)</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A liability arising from past events, such as emissions</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small);color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">A LIABILITY is RECOGNIZED when EVENTS (e.g. EMISSIONS) occurring ON or BEFORE the REPORTING date RESULT in an ENVIRONMENTAL credit OBLIGATION – the ENTITY recognizes an ECO liability BASED on the AMOUNT of credits NEEDED to satisfy the OBLIGATION as IF the reporting DATE were the END of the COMPLIANCE period.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>The Funded and Unfunded Portions of an ECO</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Blending carrying amount and fair value across two components</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small);color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">The ECO LIABILITY is MEASURED as the CARRYING amount of the COMPLIANCE environmental CREDITS the ENTITY already HOLDS and EXPECTS to USE to settle the OBLIGATION at the REPORTING date (the "FUNDED" portion), PLUS the FAIR VALUE of the environmental CREDITS necessary to SETTLE the REMAINING "UNFUNDED" portion at the REPORTING date – a GENUINELY distinctive BLENDED measurement approach, COMBINING a cost-BASED component WITH a fair-VALUE-based component WITHIN the SAME liability.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Presentation – No Netting of Credits Against Obligations</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Assets and liabilities presented gross</div><div style="font-size: var(--text-small);color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">ENVIRONMENTAL credit ASSETS and ENVIRONMENTAL credit OBLIGATION liabilities are PRESENTED separately on the BALANCE sheet – NETTING is NOT permitted, EVEN where a COMPANY holds CREDITS specifically INTENDED to settle a RECOGNIZED ECO liability, ENSURING readers can SEE the GROSS scale of BOTH the entity's HELD credits and ITS outstanding COMPLIANCE obligations.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Worked Example – Recognizing a Compliance Credit Asset</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Cost basis, no subsequent remeasurement</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Purchasing carbon allowances for compliance</div><div class="wk-body">A power company purchases carbon allowances for $2,400,000, probable of being used to settle its regulatory compliance obligation for the current period.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company recognizes an environmental CREDIT asset of <strong>$2,400,000</strong> (its COST), with NO subsequent REMEASUREMENT for MARKET price CHANGES in the ALLOWANCES – the ASSET remains AT this FIXED cost BASIS until USED to settle the ECO.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Worked Example – Measuring an Environmental Credit Obligation</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Combining a funded and unfunded component</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A partially funded compliance obligation</div><div class="wk-body">A manufacturer's emissions during the year require 100,000 compliance credits to settle. The company already holds 60,000 credits with a carrying amount of $1,800,000 (the funded portion). The remaining 40,000 credits needed have a fair value of $50 per credit.</div><div class="wk-answer">The ECO liability = FUNDED portion ($1,800,000, at CARRYING amount) + UNFUNDED portion (40,000 × $50 = $2,000,000, at FAIR value) = <strong>$3,800,000</strong>, PRESENTED as a SEPARATE liability, NOT netted AGAINST the $1,800,000 credit ASSET already HELD.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASC 818 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Nature of environmental credit programs the entity participates in, and its intended use of credits held</span><span>Carrying amounts of environmental credits and ECOs, and the line items in which they are presented</span><span>Basis for measuring the unfunded portion of an ECO, and significant estimates and assumptions used</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgment matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether a held credit is probable of being used to settle an ECO or transferred in an exchange transaction (asset recognition) versus expensed</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Fair value of environmental credits needed to settle the unfunded portion of an ECO, particularly absent an active market</span><span>Impairment assessment for exchange-intended credits recognized as assets</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Comparison to IAS 20 / ASBE 16 Government Grant Models</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A genuinely distinct model, purpose-built for tradable environmental instruments</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASC 818</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 20 / ASBE 16 (government grants)</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Core measurement basis</span><span>Cost, with intent-driven recognition; fair value only for the unfunded ECO portion</span><span>Deferred income, amortized over the useful life of a related asset or matched to compensated costs</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Obligation-side liability model</span><span>Dedicated ECO liability, blending cost and fair value</span><span>No direct equivalent – grants are income-side only</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">ASC 818 is a GENUINELY purpose-BUILT model for TRADABLE environmental CREDIT markets – NOT simply a US GAAP EQUIVALENT of the government GRANT standards SEEN elsewhere in this LIBRARY, since it ADDRESSES both the ASSET (credit) and LIABILITY (obligation) sides TOGETHER.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every environmental credit event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Compliance credit recognized</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span></span><span>At cost, no subsequent remeasurement</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>ECO liability recognized</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge is">IS</span></span><span>Funded portion at carrying amount, unfunded portion at fair value</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s17"><span class="num">17</span><h2>Related Topics</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Topic</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASC 820, Fair Value Measurement</span><span>Supplies the fair value methodology for measuring the unfunded portion of an ECO</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASC 832, Government Assistance</span><span>Addresses disclosure of government assistance more broadly; environmental credit programs may also touch this Topic where a government transaction is involved</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s18"><span class="num">18</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Environmental credit obligation (ECO)</div><div class="glossary-def">A liability arising from events (such as emissions) occurring on or before the reporting date, requiring settlement with environmental credits.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Funded / unfunded portion</div><div class="glossary-def">The funded portion of an ECO is measured at the carrying amount of credits already held; the unfunded portion is measured at the fair value of credits still needed.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

    <Glossary entries={[
      { term: "Environmental credit obligation (ECO)", definition: "A liability arising from events (such as emissions) occurring on or before the reporting date, requiring settlement with environmental credits." },
      { term: "Funded / unfunded portion", definition: "The funded portion of an ECO is measured at the carrying amount of credits already held; the unfunded portion is measured at the fair value of credits still needed." }
    ]} />

    <FinancialStatementKey />

  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asc818 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
